{
  "dom_id": "step-138218",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Converting Left-Bounded Intervals to Inequalities",
  "problem": "What inequality corresponds the interval $x\\in\\left[5, \\infty\\right)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The statement $x\\in\\left[5, \\infty\\right)$ means that $x$ lies between $5$ and $\\infty,$ where \n\n- the left endpoint $5$ *is* included, and\n\n- the right endpoint $\\infty$ is *not* included.\n\nTherefore, the inequality represented by this interval is \n\n$$\n5 \\leq   x <     \\infty.\n$$\n\nHowever, since all numbers are smaller than infinity, it suffices to write \n\n$$\n5 \\leq   x\n$$\n\nor, equivalently, \n\n$$\nx \\geq 5.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
